<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Europe</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:52Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-eu" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-1433?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-eu" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cfb1b7d90033ef1e62b90041f7790ec0e333076a82d667a570d879125f1b00ad</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:052161c43fed9a2043fc20a2efd73ab27991c155600acc1d4956486d286d1a6d</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T11:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A worker at a plague research institute in Siberia has died, and nearly 200 of her contacts are under medical observation. Russian authorities deny a link to the bacterial infection. The US is monitoring the situation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia election: New steps to prevent electoral fraud, but nationalist parties remain on top</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:55991989a03c5e76a7d7918094eb1fd4e12946ed886771dc31329a5e51a8062d</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717--5102b97990e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New technology has stopped votes being cast on behalf of dead or absent voters, and turnout has fallen to a record low. But it was a case of deja vu in Bosnia's elections with the same parties winning.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hundreds of French schools shut, teen loses hand in protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9ebed528f4b866fd0e29aa3d289a8e3b4d6faaecb6b7abbc3ba976690e35382a</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T05:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-french-schools-shut-teen-loses-hand-in-protests/a-79542656--d9ec9cc932b7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hundreds-of-french-schools-shut-teen-loses-hand-in-protests/a-79542656?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The student protests that rocked France last week have prompted authorities to keep up to 500 schools closed on Monday. A teenage boy lost his hand, seemingly while trying to pick up a police tear gas grenade.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Nationalists top Bosnia-Herzegovina's divisive election</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7cdebc2737319af5a8bae3209bb33cba5fe080cb0246d16915b80bff849c3f81</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-04T22:55:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nationalists-top-bosnia-herzegovina-s-divisive-election/a-79535336--ff55c4d27908.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nationalists-top-bosnia-herzegovina-s-divisive-election/a-79535336?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia-Herzegovina's three-member presidency is set to be dominated by nationalists from the three major ethnic groups, including Zeljka ​Cvijanovic, backed by disqualified Serb secessionist leader Milorad Dodik.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK remands 2 Iranians over alleged antisemitic terror plot</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2b60848aa210acb404d587c0fa727d957d205ec8bc70cc61fb64e921fc20c7fe</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T16:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-remands-2-iranians-over-alleged-antisemitic-terror-plot/a-79532184--b38b3689556f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-remands-2-iranians-over-alleged-antisemitic-terror-plot/a-79532184?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The pair were arrested on the eve of Yom Kippur and later charged with plotting to attack Jewish targets in Manchester.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia and Herzegovina is still shaped by war, separatism, EU ambitions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f921413b1f4650629510185e60b17dc47a467f9227d6e1824f3f5013bfa5bb4b</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-03T06:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-is-still-shaped-by-war-separatism-eu-ambitions/a-79523557--c6b59bb6d492.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-and-herzegovina-is-still-shaped-by-war-separatism-eu-ambitions/a-79523557?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia and Herzegovina is governed by a system established after the Bosnian war — more than 30 years ago. Ethnic divisions, a complex administration and European integration all shape the country's political reality.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Spain's parliament rejects housing bill as protests continue</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3c6562be3d15071e29b7dd2faa6d0b49762e0305ea07bc4962934ec37e5e0b9a</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T16:39:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-s-parliament-rejects-housing-bill-as-protests-continue/a-79522683--f3b2b2f36991.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-s-parliament-rejects-housing-bill-as-protests-continue/a-79522683?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's minority government suffered defeat in parliament as it tried to push through a pair of emergency measures aimed at making housing more affordable. A pensioner's eviction and protests led to the bid.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine, South Korea clash over transfer of 2 North Korean prisoners</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b489c7b10c9ce9a45b8e22e9945986fea386fea06ee4fe4a4b4e5869fddb32db</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T04:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-south-korea-clash-over-transfer-of-2-north-korean-prisoners/a-79508601--363762584d93.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-south-korea-clash-over-transfer-of-2-north-korean-prisoners/a-79508601?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A diplomatic scandal has erupted over two North Korean prisoners of war, with South Korea demanding an apology from Ukraine. What's been the reaction in Kyiv?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Turkey: Stock market scandal hits half a million investors</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d35f264b7d6dcfb867c32b319fd2c202948f1fbd0d3e74d4f4ceacb2a8c6206b</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T04:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710--a0311f00dcbd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/turkey-stock-market-scandal-hits-half-a-million-investors/a-79494710?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Asset managers are alleged to have artificially inflated the value of their funds. Turkish authorities have made multiple arrests, and a leading AKP lawmaker has resigned.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>EU ministers mull new ways to curb irregular migration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:de8328808c2bac0946ebf6b22339d35c0f7426fe4fef96f2c8b75018521c6b84</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T00:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-ministers-mull-new-ways-to-curb-irregular-migration/a-79509375--720c002ac8dc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-ministers-mull-new-ways-to-curb-irregular-migration/a-79509375?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The proposals include setting up so-called return hubs outside the EU and strengthening the border agency Frontex. Greece has even proposed temporarily suspending asylum applications in emergency situations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Latvians head to the polls with Russia on their minds</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:11cae6845b68347aacfc2529430995f4b311d431892fce27af8e4a8e233f51a5</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T17:57:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/on-october-3-latvians-will-elect-a-new-parliament-_-with-russia-looming-large-over-the-campaign/a-79477614--649e559e634d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/latvians-head-to-the-polls-with-russia-on-their-minds/a-79477614?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">On October 3, Latvians will elect a new parliament with Russia looming large over the campaign. Security fears dominate the agenda, but so does a debate over the economic cost of cutting ties with Moscow.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>France: Hundreds arrested as student protests escalate</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:aae2979c63a8404547e676fe5a9290f9d9e81ec04a1684f9fc9879304fda5bce</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T23:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633--b363f8aabae5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/france-hundreds-arrested-as-student-protests-escalate/a-79495633?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Student protests have grown in scale and intensity, with violent clashes in some places leading to hundreds of arrests and dozens of injuries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Five EU states plan first deportation center in Africa for 2027</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:99a7068f25b069ef933b66b946699c925cc0e722efd605820ab432217994aaa8</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T19:16:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162--dbd1d60c3bb2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/five-eu-states-plan-first-deportation-center-in-africa-for-2027/a-79490162?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Greece, Germany, Austria, Denmark and the Netherlands are moving forward with plans to establish deportation centers for rejected asylum seekers outside the EU.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia elections: Polls overshadowed by exhaustion, exodus and geopolitics as ethnic politics eclipse real problems</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c0eeb9e61a6e395b08c9b862d76e9078ebfbb73d4852e48693eec8892423315a</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T12:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-/a-79487802--91e658c381f3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-elections-polls-overshadowed-by-exhaustion-exodus-and-geopolitics-as-ethnic-politics-eclipse-real-problems/a-79487802?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Bosnia goes to the polls on October 4 to elect several parliaments and presidents. While voters worry about the economy and emigration, the campaign is focused on ethnicity, exposing the country's political paralysis.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ireland will boycott Eurovision again because of Israel's participation, but the song contest is still expanding</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd5255e65216fdefc285f9026a169e28ffaa9155ea2fa6611482a990103ec144</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T09:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-stil/a-79401752--f96894bb90e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ireland-will-boycott-eurovision-again-because-of-israel-s-participation-but-the-song-contest-is-still-expanding/a-79401752?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2026 Eurovision Song Contest was marred by boycotts in protest against Israel's participation in the midst of its war on Gaza. It still aims to keep growing.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary's reckoning with Orban's corrupt system picks up speed</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1f75c02dff29f77d46c735a1173d76fc3b3349947b3761e20c41addf33afc281</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-30T04:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed/a-79473714--fef6c98dbd47.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-s-reckoning-with-orban-s-corrupt-system-picks-up-speed/a-79473714?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Hungary's Prime Minister Peter Magyar vowed to dismantle Orban's corrupt networks. High-profile figures are being arrested and many Hungarians are pushing for swift accountability, but the rule of law takes time.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK PM Burnham seeks 'hope again' at Labour Party conference</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:497a341b40c058693f846f989248513b7d129b198bb763cd31a95d3b23d77ca6</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T13:38:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376--71e603fc9e60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-pm-burnham-seeks-hope-again-at-labour-party-conference/a-79473376?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Andy Burnham is seeking a delicate balance between optimism and realism at Labour's annual party conference. He promised hope and an end to "politics as usual" but also an "honest conversation" about difficult dilemmas.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Albania: As corruption cases multiply, experts question whether the anti-corruption drive is addressing the causes or just the symptoms.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:26d9de5b08c567789b92574630fa5286610b9d0209cd807aea9d9e9195ffdf6e</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T11:59:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/albania-as-corruption-cases-multiply-experts-question-whether-the-anti-corruption-drive-is-addressin/a-79473031--8c7e71b0b3b6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/albania-as-corruption-cases-multiply-experts-question-whether-the-anti-corruption-drive-is-addressing-the-causes-or-just-the-symptoms/a-79473031?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">From a former president to the ex-intelligence chief, Albania is prosecuting senior officials at a rate once thought impossible. But do more prosecutions mean less corruption or simply better enforcement?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>UK: US government questions bail for Fairford base suspects</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7d119cd2ded7ecfd154cbdb4d1b654fa996149fdfeb10522ede6febafc523d89</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:42Z</updated><published>2026-09-29T08:17:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-us-government-questions-bail-for-fairford-base-suspects/a-79468803--3794b4b54f63.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-us-government-questions-bail-for-fairford-base-suspects/a-79468803?maca=en-rss-en-eu-2092-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US government sees "the hand of a foreign actor" in the security scare at RAF Fairford, a hub for US heavy bombers in Europe. Donald Trump criticized the suspects being released on bail amid ongoing investigations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry></feed>
